9:     A canonical example of a LabelImage is a brain label_image or parcellation.\n650: \n651:     This class provides convenient functionality for manipulating and visualizing\n652:     images where you have real values associated with aggregated image regions (e.g.\n653:     if you have cortical thickness values associated with brain regions)\n654: \n655:     Commonly-used functionality for LabelImage types:\n656:         - create publication-quality figures of an label_image\n657: \n658:     Nomenclature\n659:     ------------\n660:     - key : a string representing the name of the associated index in the atlas image\n661:         - e.g. if the index is 1001 and the key may be InferiorTemporalGyrus`\n662:     - value : an integer value in the atlas image\n663:     - metakey : a string representing one of the possible sets of label key\n664:         - e.g. 'Lobes' or 'Regions'\n665:     Notes\n666:     -----\n667:     - indexing works by creating a separate dict for each metakey, where\n668:     \"\"\"\n669:     def __init__(self, label_image, label_info=None, template=None):\n670:         \"\"\"\n671:         Initialize a LabelImage\n672: \n673:         ANTsR function: N/A\n674: \n675:         Arguments\n676:         ---------\n677:         label_image : ANTsImage\n678:             discrete (integer) image as label_image\n679: \n680:         label_info : dict or pandas.DataFrame\n681:             mapping between discrete values in `image` and string names\n682:             - if dict, the keys should be the discrete integer label values\n683:               and the values should be the label names or another dict with\n684:               any metadata\n685:             - if pd.DataFrame, the index (df.index) should be the discrete integer\n686:               label values and the other column(s) should be the label names and\n687:               any metadata\n688: \n689:         template : ANTsImage\n690:             default real-valued image to use for plotting or c