ngWindowedSinc\n48:             lanczosWindowedSinc\n49:             genericLabel use this for label images\n50: \n51:     imagetype : integer\n52:         choose 0/1/2/3 mapping to scalar/vector/tensor/time-series\n53: \n54:     whichtoinvert : list of booleans (optional)\n55:         Must be same length as transformlist.\n56:         whichtoinvert[i] is True if transformlist[i] is a matrix,\n57:         and the matrix should be inverted. If transformlist[i] is a\n58:         warp field, whichtoinvert[i] must be False.\n59:         If the transform list is a matrix followed by a warp field,\n60:         whichtoinvert defaults to (True,False). Otherwise it defaults\n61:         to [False]*len(transformlist)).\n62: \n63:     compose : string (optional)\n64:         if it is a string pointing to a valid file location,\n65:         this will force the function to return a composite transformation filename.\n66: \n67:     defaultvalue : scalar\n68:         Default voxel value for mappings outside the image domain.\n69: \n70:     verbose : boolean\n71:         print command and run verbose application of transform.\n72: \n73:     singleprecision : boolean\n74:         if True, perform the transformation in single precision (float32).\n75:         if False (default), perform the transformation in double precision (float64).\n76:         The returned image will always have the same pixeltype as the moving image.\n77: \n78:     kwargs : keyword arguments\n79:         extra parameters\n80: \n81:     Returns\n82:     -------\n83:     ANTsImage or string (transformation filename)\n84: \n85:     Example\n86:     -------\n87:     >>> import ants\n88:     >>> fixed = ants.image_read( ants.get_ants_data('r16') )\n89:     >>> moving = ants.image_read( ants.get_ants_data('r64') )\n90:     >>> fixed = ants.resample_image(fixed, (64,64), 1, 0)\n91:     >>> moving = ants.resample_image(moving, (64,64), 1, 0)\n92:     >>> mytx = ants.registration(fixed=fixed , moving=moving ,\n93:      